    <string name="fin_help_title">How to use</string>
    <string name="fin_help_body">RPN: type the numbers first, then the operation. ENTER separates two numbers.\n\n2 ENTER 3 +  gives 5\n\nLoan payment: 1000 CHS PV, 12 n, 1 i, 0 FV, then PMT.\nCHS changes the sign. Cash in is positive and cash out is negative, so PV and PMT must have opposite signs.\n\nPressing n, i, PV, PMT or FV after typing a number stores it. Pressing one of them again with nothing typed calculates it.\n\n2nd gives the function written above each key. STO and RCL work with memory 0-9.\n\nCash flows: CF0 for the initial flow, CFj for the next ones, Nj to repeat the last one. Set i, then NPV, or press IRR.</string>
